{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"544:- **Scan findings are not inspectable enough to act on** (reported\n545-  2026-07-27 while dogfooding turnbridge). `formatFinding` prints ~20\n546-  characters of context each side with the match itself replaced by\n547-  `<redacted>`, and there is no supported way to see the flagged event in\n548-  full — so a finding on a 26 KB conversation turn gives the user no way to\n549-  judge whether it is a real secret or a false positive, which is exactly\n550-  the decision `cledger allow` vs `cledger redact` demands. Observed case:\n551-  a turn *discussing* GitHub Actions code (`getInput(\"github-token\")`)\n552-  tripped `keyword-assignment`, and the excerpt was too narrow to tell that\n553-  from a real leak.\n554-  Constraint to respect: the zero-characters-of-the-secret rule in\n555-  `buildExcerpt` is deliberate — the report itself gets captured into a\n556-  later conversation, so printing any of the match would re-seed the\n557-  finding it describes. The fix therefore is not \"widen the excerpt\"\n558-  alone. Candidate shape:\n559-  - carry the match's JSON path in `Finding` (`walkStrings` already knows\n560-    it; it is simply discarded) and print it, so the user at least knows\n561-    *where* in the event the hit is;\n562-  - a `--context N` flag on `cledger scan` for more surrounding text, still\n563-    with the match masked;\n564-  - an explicit, clearly-labelled escape hatch — `cledger show-finding\n565-    <event-id> [--reveal]` — that writes the unmasked region to a file\n566-    outside the repo rather than to stdout, so it cannot be swept into an\n567-    agent transcript. Today the only route is `cledger export` piped\n568-    through a hand-written filter.\n569-  `scripts/inspect-finding.py` is a throwaway prototype of the last two,\n570-  kept only as reference for whoever implements this properly.\n571-- Whether an explicit `Conversation` manifest object earns its keep once\n572-  multiple producers exist.\n573-- Reads deliberately do *not* walk the notes ref's history; only the tip tree\n574-  is authoritative. Unioning across history was proposed and set aside because\n=== version ===\n  \"version\": \"0.15.0\",\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/.claude/worktrees/spec-verification-gaps","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Uzb3QbwKKdCqjMNMt8aaY","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"8bc736298158ee25b1c78cfc1537dc20e9392a15","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:a6b0721f-3d36-4802-bc44-520ed792e1b6","seq":1246},"id":"ev1-48d30f0c8caf0f1e9a13a173e38757a0a7acab9fac25d79ad0083a771a3cba26","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-30T14:41:37.995Z","producer":{"session_id":"a6b0721f-3d36-4802-bc44-520ed792e1b6","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.220","tool":"cledger","version":"0.16.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/.claude/worktrees/spec-verification-gaps","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-spec-verification-gaps","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"544:- **Scan findings are not inspectable enough to act on** (reported\n545-  2026-07-27 while dogfooding turnbridge). `formatFinding` prints ~20\n546-  characters of context each side with the match itself replaced by\n547-  `<redacted>`, and there is no supported way to see the flagged event in\n548-  full — so a finding on a 26 KB conversation turn gives the user no way to\n549-  judge whether it is a real secret or a false positive, which is exactly\n550-  the decision `cledger allow` vs `cledger redact` demands. Observed case:\n551-  a turn *discussing* GitHub Actions code (`getInput(\"github-token\")`)\n552-  tripped `keyword-assignment`, and the excerpt was too narrow to tell that\n